<article class="env-definition" id="01T5">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01T5">Definition <span data-tag="01T5">5.1.1.1</span>.</a> Let $q: X \rightarrow S$ be a morphism of simplicial sets, and let $e$ be an edge of $X$. We say that $e$ is <em>$q$-cartesian</em> if every lifting problem </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \Lambda ^{n}_{n} \ar [r]^-{\sigma _0} \ar [d] &amp;  X \ar [d]^-{q} \\ \Delta ^ n \ar [r]^-{ \overline{\sigma } } \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur] &amp;  S } \]
</div>
<p> admits a solution, provided that $n \geq 2$ and the composite map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^1 \simeq \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \{  n-1 &lt; n \}  ) \hookrightarrow \Lambda ^ n_{n} \xrightarrow {\sigma _0} X \]
</div>
<p> corresponds to the edge $e$. </p>
<p>We say that $e$ is <em>$q$-cocartesian</em> if every lifting problem </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ \Lambda ^{n}_{0} \ar [r]^-{\sigma _0} \ar [d] &amp;  X \ar [d]^-{q} \\ \Delta ^ n \ar [r]^-{ \overline{\sigma } } \ar@ {--&gt;}[ur] &amp;  S } \]
</div>
<p> admits a solution, provided that $n \geq 2$ and the composite map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^1 \simeq \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \{  0 &lt; 1 \}  ) \hookrightarrow \Lambda ^ n_{0} \xrightarrow {\sigma _0} X \]
</div>
<p> corresponds to the edge $e$. </p>
</article>
